		<title>Perplexity&#039;s new Monitor API turns web search from a one-off query into a nonstop watchdog</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/perplexitys-new-monitor-api-turns-web-search-from-a-one-off-query-into-a-nonstop-watchdog/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/perplexitys-new-monitor-api-turns-web-search-from-a-one-off-query-into-a-nonstop-watchdog/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jonathan Kemper]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:20:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI search]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Perplexity]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=43193</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Perplexity-Logo-Silhouette-Nano-Banana-Pro.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="Bright blue, geometric Perplexity AI logo on a dark background" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        Perplexity is launching a Monitor API that searches the web on a schedule and alerts agents via webhook only when relevant changes occur. Its own decision model filters out unimportant results. For Perplexity, the API is part of a broader strategy to stand out from an increasingly interchangeable chatbot business through developer tools.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/perplexitys-new-monitor-api-turns-web-search-from-a-one-off-query-into-a-nonstop-watchdog/">Perplexity&#039;s new Monitor API turns web search from a one-off query into a nonstop watchdog</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
